Z||000007||pontiacs4me||05-27-2001||09:59 PM||||The intercoolers for the 3800 supercharged go under the blower, like mentioned above.  A friend of mine has a 3800 sc in a 1991 lumina 4 door.  He hasnt coughed up the money for the intercooler yet, but he does estimate that his car makes 350 horse at the crank.  He custom makes phenolic throttle body spacers, for his nitrous.  And he has an overdrive pulley also.  Besides other intake and exhaust mods.  He is running a 70 shot, and 2 weekends ago he turned a 12.87 at 111 mph.  His car weighs 3550 with him in it, and it gets 26 mpg on the highway.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jaei Sun||05-27-2001||10:39 PM||||Will it fit inside a "normal" fiero??  Looking at pictures of it from the Thrasher site it raises up the blower a few inches.  Will it fit under the decklid/heat vents??<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000009||pontiacs4me||05-27-2001||10:45 PM||||You will probably have to make a custom scoop for the decklid, there wont be any problems with the vents, but the hump in the deck probably isnt big enough.  Just get a mustang style scoop, and it will be fine.||||reg||1
